---
source: crates/nage/tests/cli.rs
expression: transcript
---
$ nage init --help
[stdout]
Set Nage up at the terminal: the book, its currency and the first user, an admin

Usage: nage init [OPTIONS] --book-name <NAME> --currency <CODE> --username <NAME> --display-name <NAME>

Options:
      --data-dir <DIR>       The data folder, created with its backups folder and the database when they are missing [env: NAGE_DATA_DIR] [default: ./data]
      --book-name <NAME>     The book's name, such as Household
      --currency <CODE>      The book's currency, a code such as CAD; it never changes afterwards, so there is no default
      --username <NAME>      The username of the first user, who is an admin
      --display-name <NAME>  The first user's display name
      --no-starter-accounts  Leave the starter accounts out
      --password-stdin       Read the password once from standard input instead of asking for it twice at the terminal
  -h, --help                 Print help
[stderr]
[exit] 0
